                <pb facs="0312" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg270"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Agreement made at
                                <placeName>Liverpool</placeName></hi>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >this</hi> 28<hi rendition="#italic">th day of March,</hi>
                            1863</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Ten days after the ship Japan sails from the river Clyde the undersigned do
                    hereby promise and agree to pay to any person who shall advance two pounds ten
                    shillings---------pence to Edward Davis, on this agreement, the sum of two
                    pounds ten shillings---------pence, provided the said Edward Davis shall sail in
                    the said ship from the said river Clyde.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JONES &amp; CO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Payable at 28 Chapel street.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
